*------------------------------------------------------------------------------
* D-2 witness (GREEN -- same graph without the deferred capture call).  The SECOND claws5 defect, isolated: a DEFERRED CAPTURE
* CALL -- `. *token()` -- on an ALT arm inside ARBNO.  Run with SCRIP_SPAN_FRAME=1
* so the s130/s131 leaf-suspension class (the FIRST defect, cured by that arm) is
* out of the way; what remains is m4-only.  rt_dcap_pump reaches the SNOBOL-defined
* target through rt_call_proc_descr's by-name dyn transfer, which in a mode-4 image
* lands on a bogus address (the s156 by-name-dispatch class, D-18's rung).
* Oracle (SPITBOL x64/bin/sbl -b) and SCRIP mode-3 agree; SCRIP mode-4 SIG11s.
*------------------------------------------------------------------------------
        DEFINE('token()')  :(token_end)
token   n       =   n + 1
        token   =   .dummy  :(NRETURN)
token_end
        &TRIM   =   0
        n       =   0
        src     =   'ab_A0 ab_A0 ab_A0 ab_A0 ab_A0 ab_A0 ab_A0 ab_A0 ab_A0 '
        p       =   POS(0) ARBNO((SPAN('0123456789') | SPAN('ab') SPAN('_A0')) SPAN(' ')) RPOS(0)
        src     ?   p  :F(error)
        OUTPUT  =   'matched bytes=' SIZE(src) ' n=' n  :(END)
error   OUTPUT  =   'Pattern match failed'
END
